{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "duo_recon_vm_g1",
    "description": "Chen (2021) fixed-coefficient polynomial reconstruction of the EAST-side cell-face midpoint value on an Nc = 2*Ng-1 = 1-point stencil from volume-mean variables (Ng = 1 ghost layers; Table 2 row). eta^E = sum_l c_l a_l with c = [1@l=0] over offsets l = -(Ng-1)..(Ng-1); the coefficients sum to 1 (constant-preserving) and reproduce the true face value to design order 1 on a smooth field (numerically verified: Ng=1,2,3 -> order 1,3,5). AXIS- AND DIRECTION-NEUTRAL scalar algebra: this atom knows nothing about x/y or which tile edge. The consumer places it at any of the four faces by binding the params to the appropriate neighbour gathers on the halo-EXTENDED field (grids/duo/rules/duo_extend), where the 1-D duo-grid alignment makes every interface -- interior and tile-seam alike -- a uniform interior stencil with no one-sided closure. EAST face of cell i: a_l <- q_{i+l}. WEST face of cell i uses the paper's mirror gamma^W_l = gamma^E_{-l}: bind a_l <- q_{i-l} (params reversed). NORTH/SOUTH are the same two binding patterns along the y axis. Rational coefficients are emitted as exact integer divisions so every binding evaluates the identical IEEE double. No limiter (this work implements no monotonic filter); Nc = 1, stencil symmetric with reach Ng-1 = 0.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:stencil",
      "family:finite_volume",
      "grid:duo",
      "op:reconstruct",
      "order:1",
      "scheme:volumemean",
      "stencil_width:1"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Chen, X. (2021). The LMARS based shallow-water dynamical core on generic gnomonic cubed sphere geometry. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems, 13(1), e2020MS002280. (Section 3.2, Eqs 16-19 and Tables 1-2: fixed-coefficient polynomial reconstruction to cell-face midpoints.)",
        "doi": "10.1029/2020MS002280"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Chen, X., Andronova, N., Van Leer, B., Penner, J. E., Boyd, J. P., Jablonowski, C., & Lin, S.-J. (2018). Toward an unstaggered finite-volume dynamical core with a fast Riemann solver: 1-D linearized analysis of dissipation, dispersion, and noise control. Journal of Advances in Modeling Earth Systems (source of the reconstruction coefficient tables).",
        "doi": "10.1029/2018MS001361"
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "duo_recon_vm_g1": {
      "params": [
        "a0"
      ],
      "body": "a0"
    }
  }
}
